# RUNTIME DATA of the update protocol (src/update.rs, intent item 64).
#
# THREADS_HOME points at this directory on the operator's machine — exactly as
# TTS_HOME does for lib/tts — so the daemon's own state lands beside its source.
# None of it is a repo artifact:
#
#   threads.last-good     — a 26 MB copy of the last binary known to boot, so a
#                           bad build can never leave him with no daemon.
#   pending-restart.json  — the durable queued restart and its reason.
#   restarts.jsonl        — one line per restart decision (deferred / firing /
#                           refused), so the next person can see why it waited.
threads.last-good
pending-restart.json
restarts.jsonl

# THE CONVERSATIONS THEMSELVES, and they are not small.
#
# `turns/` is the per-execution stdout the daemon streams each `claude` child
# into; `backups/` is where a repair takes its snapshot before touching a
# transcript. On the operator's machine on 2026-08-06 those were 393 MB and
# 742 MB — and they sat UNTRACKED next to source that several agents edit and
# commit with a broad `git add`. One of those sweeps had already picked up
# another agent's in-progress work that day; the only reason it did not also
# pick up a gigabyte of the operator's private conversations is that nobody
# happened to run `git add -A` while they were there.
#
# Naming them here is the cheap half of that lesson.
turns/
backups/

# Captured Claude account snapshots and the name -> CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR registry.
# Carried over from substrate's ROOT .gitignore (`lib/threads/accounts/`,
# `lib/threads/accounts.toml`) when this crate moved (R3.S2.M): per-account
# login state and machine-local paths, never a repo artifact. `add-account`
# refuses to write a snapshot that `git check-ignore` does not cover.
accounts/
accounts.toml
